<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Setskill (245)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>setskill &lt;someone&gt; skill &lt;skill&gt; &lt;value&gt;
setskill &lt;someone&gt; spell &lt;spell&gt; &lt;value&gt;
setskill &lt;someone&gt; weapon &lt;weapon&gt; &lt;value&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>setskill Gnort skill pick_lock 80
setskill Gnort spell cure_light 50
setskill guard weapon long_sword 75
</pre>
<p>Sets how well someone knows a skill, a spell or a weapon, anywhere in the 
world. Write a name of two words with an underscore (pick_lock), and you 
may shorten it from the end. You are told "New value: &lt;n&gt;".
</p><p>Only players have the full tree of spells and weapons, and only players 
have skills. Monsters have just the spheres and the weapon categories (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): giving a monster a single spell or weapon is refused. It 
is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Set</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
</pre>




</div>